{
    "_meta": {
        "id": "bikepacking",
        "name": "Bikepacking",
        "description": "The full touring map: roads by class, trails and cycleways, rail, water, forests and landuse, buildings up close.",
        "version": 5,
        "swatch": [
            "#FF5500",
            "#FFAA00",
            "#5500FF",
            "#55AAFF",
            "#55AA55",
            "#AAAAAA"
        ],
        "palette_note": "Colors are RGB565 but the LS021B7DD02 panel only shows 64 (RGB222: 4 levels/channel = 0,85,170,255). Every value below is chosen to land exactly on that grid, so the web builder picker and the device agree. OSM/Komoot conventions on a cream 'paper' base (the only near-white tint the gamut offers): warm = through-roads, white with a grey casing = local streets, brown = trails, indigo = cycleways (a cycling computer's key feature, lifted out of the brown trail group), green = vegetation, azure = water, light grey = built-up landuse fill (residential / commercial / industrial / retail — towns read as a quiet grey wash), with darker grey buildings on top at the closest zoom only. Verify the gamut with `obc-sim --palette`."
    },
